c{1}{3}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}≈0.577.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522737 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166794 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "edde1bb6-42d9-5b8d-a29b-7fa91711f017" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Standard Deviation of a Uniformly Distributed Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e1da86a-acf0-5bb3-a54c-f4594c8ca9a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.464" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522122} {:answer/id #uuid "7e01737b-1f7f-5999-938f-4812fade8196" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.887" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522266} {:answer/id #uuid "b7d5bc7c-8b5f-5c52-80eb-7ebea3034ba9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.753" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522396} {:answer/id #uuid "cf52b9fa-0250-5b04-8492-5a8dc9699ff4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.041" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522448} {:answer/id #uuid "d0eb2794-a1da-5a80-8aa1-359a3dd791bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.907" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522454}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e1da86a-acf0-5bb3-a54c-f4594c8ca9a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.464" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522122} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c2866f6-4249-5037-8e66-4f0903c1de0f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522629}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6e72c01b-4831-5832-84ce-7e36b797f77a" :question/math-academy-id "q-130725" :question/problem "Given that $X$ is a random variable such that $X∼U[-2,10],$ find $\\text{SD}[X].$ Round your answer to three decimal places." :question/worked-solution "If the random variable $X$ is distributed uniformly over the interval $[a,b],$ then \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{(b-a)^{2}}{12}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $a=-2$ and $b=10.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{(10-(-2))^{2}}{12}=\\frac{144}{12}=12.\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\text{SD}[X]=\\sqrt{12}=2\\sqrt{3}≈3.464.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186522728 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166794 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "edde1bb6-42d9-5b8d-a29b-7fa91711f017" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Standard Deviation of a Uniformly Distributed Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "099eec1e-8ed2-5113-a1c7-b3171fd7cc20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.753" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522036} {:answer/id #uuid "0c53a141-0b65-5522-b2db-8e41ad1971d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.041" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522044} {:answer/id #uuid "1075691a-f199-58c0-92cc-267e0384d912" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.330" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522050} {:answer/id #uuid "a38d747f-8549-5520-968d-5b1ecc48e36b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.887" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522360} {:answer/id #uuid "b8bff4e0-34bf-583b-859b-3da016dddf10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.907" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522399}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1075691a-f199-58c0-92cc-267e0384d912" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.330" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186522050} :answer-field/id #uuid "ad120d86-b9b1-586a-a131-2aff030ba3c4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.typ